FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/differential_test.rs:329 — `edge_a_missing_expected_output_file_is_a_runner_failure` never exercises the runner — it creates `orphan.rb`, asserts no `.expected` exists, then asserts the collected `.expected` list is empty, never calling `loaded_corpus`/`assert_outcome_matches` on the missing file — a test for a missing expectation that cannot fail — assert the missing-file load panics via `catch_unwind`.
2. [BLOCKER] tests/differential_test.rs:253 — `assert!(!writing || ...count() >= 200)` is a tautology when `RB_WRITE_CORPUS` is unset (the normal CI case) — the 200-program floor is unenforced — change to unconditional `assert!(count >= 200)`.
3. [MAJOR] tests/common/corpus.rs:153 — `assert_outcome_matches` `none` branch checks `is_ok()` and output only, and `format_expected` at tests/common/corpus.rs:55 discards the `Ok` value entirely — return-value divergences (e.g. trailing-token `say 1 2 3` → `Ok("3")` vs `Ok("nothing")` per FINDINGS §4) pass the golden check — record and compare the `Ok` payload.
4. [MAJOR] tests/common/corpus.rs:164 — `assert_outcome_matches` failing branch asserts `output == []` ("a program that fails must print nothing") — false in general; a `say` before an uncaught fault prints, which tests/property_test.rs:271 explicitly allows for `RuntimeError` — drop the assertion or allow pre-failure output.
5. [MAJOR] tests/property_test.rs:148 — `random_statement(rng, 0)` is always called with `depth 0`, so arms `(0,_)` shadow `(_,4)`/`(_,_)` and the `repeat N times ... random_statement(depth-1)` branch is unreachable — the property generator never emits loops despite claiming statement coverage — seed with `depth > 0` or restructure the match.
6. [MAJOR] tests/common/corpus.rs:118 — `escape` covers only `\` and `\n`, so a program printing `#message foo` is written verbatim and `parse_expected` at tests/common/corpus.rs:90 re-parses it as the failure-message line (or panics per tests/common/corpus.rs:100 for `label none`) — escape/prefix output lines or frame the file unambiguously.
7. [MINOR] tests/common/vm.rs:26 — `failure_of` compares only `label: message`, discarding span/line-column by design (tests/common/vm.rs:19) — an error-line regression is invisible to both corpus and differential checks — include the span in `Outcome` or assert it separately.
8. [MINOR] tests/common/rng.rs:57 — `pick` documents "must not be empty" but indexes `items[self.below(items.len())]` where `below(0)==0`, so an empty slice panics on `items[0]` — add `assert!(!items.is_empty())` with a message.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 8
